- If it can''t be reused: say why in `AGENTS.md` ("Commands") and add a follow-up task (`pm task add 8 …`) for what it would take; note in `docs/luv-wishlist.md` what luv could export to make it reusable.

## Done when
- The loop was run end to end once (two screenshots read, showing the change), or the reason it can''t be is written down with a follow-up task; no image or window left running; files staged.', '2026-10-14T16:16:09Z', '2026-10-14T17:23:48Z', 15, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (27, 8, 'AGENTS.md Commands, verified from a clean clone; skeleton decisions recorded', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, AGENTS.md (Commands, Layout); verified from a clean clone: nix build 17 s (luv from cache), nix run opens the window, scripts/test 18/18 ~5 s, scripts/screenshot with and without display ~3 s, ./sly start/play/screenshot/eval/stop ~5 s start; decision 9, decision 10, consequence on decision 8. Seen: luv''s sly-client prints a literal ~% after ''No failures are retained'' (luv bug, scripts/sly-client.lisp:2293 upstream; relevant to task 28)', 'Part of `plan 8: walking skeleton`, its last task: fill in the "Commands" section of `AGENTS.md` and prove each command works from a clean checkout.

## Do
- `AGENTS.md` "Commands": replace "to be filled in by `milestone 1`" with one bullet each for: dev shell, build (`nix build`), run (`nix run`), test (`scripts/test` or what the test task made), screenshot, live image (or why there is none). Keep the existing style (concise bullets).
- Verify: `git clone` the repo (HEAD holds the earlier tasks'' work; your uncommitted `AGENTS.md` edit isn''t needed there) into `$(mktemp -d)`, run each command there (close every window), note the time of a cold `nix build`/first run in `AGENTS.md`, delete the clone.
- Record the lasting choices with `pm decision record`, citing what they rely on:
  - layout of systems and directories (`luv-in-space.asd`, `src/`, `tests/`, `scripts/`);
  - the test command and the screenshot command (paths, arguments, headless or windowed);
  - the dev loop (live image wrapper, or none and why).
- Fix small breakages found in the clean clone; larger ones become follow-up tasks in `plan 8: walking skeleton`.

## Done when
- Every command in "Commands" ran from the clean clone; decisions recorded; `AGENTS.md` staged; clone deleted; no process left running.', '2026-10-14T16:16:09Z', '2026-10-14T17:25:52Z', 15, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (28, 8, 'Live image: report failed live artifacts', 'work', 'done', 790, '2026-10-14, src/main.lisp, src/package.lisp, scripts/sly-client.lisp, tests/package.lisp, AGENTS.md, docs/luv-capabilities.md, docs/luv-wishlist.md: ./sly status prints failed live artifacts via luv-in-space:report-failed-live-artifacts; checked live with a broken earth fragment method (named, error shown, gone after fix)', 'Part of `plan 8: walking skeleton`, after `task 26: Live image dev loop for luv-in-space`.

luv''s live image keeps the last good pipeline when a shader redefinition fails and reports the failure nowhere but `luv:live-artifact-diagnostic` of the application''s live artifacts (status `:failed`); `./sly status` and `./sly failures` stay silent (`docs/luv-capabilities.md`, "Live image and dev loop", run 21; listed in `docs/luv-wishlist.md`).

## Do
- In this repo''s live-image setup from `task 26: Live image dev loop for luv-in-space`: make `status` (or `failures`) also print every failed live artifact of the running game with its diagnostic; if task 26 found the live image can''t be reused, a Lisp function the agent calls with `eval` instead.
- Check it: while the game plays, redefine a shader function with an unknown operator; the command names the shader and the error; fix it and the report is gone.
- Document the command in `AGENTS.md` "Commands".

## Done when
- The broken-shader check above was run; no image or window left running; files staged.', '2026-10-14T16:59:23Z', '2026-10-14T17:36:26Z', 21, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (29, 8, 'Darwin build: Objective-C bridge outside luv''s read-only source', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, flake.nix, docs/luv-wishlist.md: on aarch64-darwin luv loads from a writable copy (package $out/share/luv pruned to build/ bridge dylib and objective-c/ as luv''s applicationPackage does; dev shell ${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-~/.cache}/luv-in-space/luv-<shortRev>; check $TMPDIR/luv). Linux derivations byte-identical (same drv paths); nix flake check --no-build --all-systems passes; nix build and scripts/test pass. Darwin build untested: no Apple Silicon machine (decision 6: Target platforms).', 'Part of `plan 8: walking skeleton`. `task 22: Flake: luv input, dev shell, package and nix run opening an empty window` builds the game against luv''s sources straight from the flake input (`${luv}/` on `CL_SOURCE_REGISTRY` in `flake.nix`). On `aarch64-darwin`, luv''s `objective-c/exception-bridge.lisp` compiles a dylib to `<luv source>/../build/objective-c-exception-bridge-<stamp>.dylib`, i.e. into the read-only Nix store path, so `nix build` and loading `luv-in-space` in the dev shell will fail there. luv''s own `applicationPackage` avoids this by copying its tree into `$out/share/luv` and keeping `build/` and `objective-c/` on Darwin.

## Do
- In `flake.nix`, on Darwin only (`lib.optionalString pkgs.stdenv.hostPlatform.isDarwin`): copy `${luv}` into a writable directory (package: `$out/share/luv`, kept with its `build/` and `objective-c/` as luv''s recipe does; dev shell: a cache directory, e.g. `${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-$HOME/.cache}/luv-in-space/luv-<rev>`) and put that on `CL_SOURCE_REGISTRY` instead of `${luv}/`.
- Keep Linux unchanged.
- Verify with `nix flake check --no-build --all-systems`; a real build needs an Apple Silicon machine (`decision 6: Target platforms`: Darwin is evaluated only), so note it as untested if none is available.
- The wishlist entry already exists in `docs/luv-wishlist.md` (Objective-C bridge output directory).', '2026-10-14T17:08:42Z', '2026-10-14T17:28:42Z', 22, 0);
INSERT INTO task (id, plan_id, subject, kind, status, priority, note, body, created_at, retired_at, created_by_task, web) VALUES (30, 8, 'Live shader pipelines for the scene', 'work', 'done', NULL, '2026-10-14, src/scene.lisp, src/shaders.lisp, src/main.lisp, AGENTS.md, docs/luv-capabilities.md', 'Part of `plan 8: walking skeleton`, follow-up of `task 26: Live image dev loop for luv-in-space`: shader redefinitions while playing in `./sly` should show on the next frame.

## Now
- `src/scene.lisp` `make-scene` calls the shader functions (`luv-in-space.shaders::earth-fragment` …) once and builds plain pipelines; a `define-shader` re-evaluated through `./sly eval` changes nothing on screen until `./sly stop-playing` and `./sly play` (`docs/luv-capabilities.md`, live image, run 34).
- luv''s Luft refreshes its pipelines live: a redefined shader function changed the next frame (run 20). luv exports `make-live-shader-pipeline`, `refresh-live-shader-pipeline`, `live-shader-pipeline-native-pipeline`, `application-live-artifacts` (`../luv/hal/package.lisp`, read-only reference; see how Luft uses them).

## Do
- Build the Earth and overlay pipelines as luv live shader pipelines (or the equivalent luv uses), registered as the game''s live artifacts, so a redefined shader is picked up while playing.
- Verify with `./sly`: play, screenshot, redefine `earth-fragment` (e.g. red oceans) by `./sly eval`, screenshot again, read both; stop playing and stop the image by `./sly stop`.
- A broken redefinition keeps the last good pipeline; reporting it is `task 28: Live image: report failed live artifacts`.
- `scripts/test` and `scripts/screenshot` still pass; update the live image bullet in `AGENTS.md` "Commands".', '2026-10-14T17:23:16Z', '2026-10-14T17:30:44Z', 26, 0);
